        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.58,
          "en": "This course section will build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.58,
          "end": 7.14,
          "en": "up on the previous course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.14,
          "end": 9.1,
          "en": "Now, in that previous section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.1,
          "end": 13.02,
          "en": "we learned a lot about building real React Native apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.02,
          "end": 15.37,
          "en": "how we can build nice layouts and styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.37,
          "end": 19.29,
          "en": "and combine multiple components, custom components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.29,
          "end": 23.6,
          "en": "and built-in components to build real mobile apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.6,
          "end": 24.943,
          "en": "with React Native.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.79,
          "end": 28.57,
          "en": "In this course section, we're going to learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.57,
          "end": 30.85,
          "en": "how we can make our mobile apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.85,
          "end": 35.85,
          "en": "and our mobile user interfaces more adaptive and responsive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.43,
          "end": 40.38,
          "en": "how we can build apps that adapt to different platforms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.38,
          "end": 43.09,
          "en": "and different device sizes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.09,
          "end": 47.36,
          "en": "and how we can, for example, write platform-specific code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.36,
          "end": 50.45,
          "en": "which means that we generally have one code based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.45,
          "end": 53.28,
          "en": "for both iOS and Android, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.28,
          "end": 56.76,
          "en": "but that in some cases we can differentiate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.76,
          "end": 60.9,
          "en": "between those platforms and execute slightly different code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.9,
          "end": 63.77,
          "en": "based on which platform we're running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.77,
          "end": 66.24,
          "en": "In addition, we're going to learn how we can adjust",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.24,
          "end": 68.25,
          "en": "to different device sizes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.25,
          "end": 70.92,
          "en": "and for example, update our styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.92,
          "end": 74.99,
          "en": "or our layout based on the available width and height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.99,
          "end": 77.67,
          "en": "And we're going to learn how we can also React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.67,
          "end": 80.78,
          "en": "to the screen orientation chosen by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.78,
          "end": 84.73,
          "en": "In general, the idea behind this course section is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.73,
          "end": 87.86,
          "en": "to teach you a broad variety of tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.86,
          "end": 91.05,
          "en": "that you have to adjust your interface as needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.05,
          "end": 94.78,
          "en": "and to teach you how you can build adaptive components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.78,
          "end": 97.50999999999999,
          "en": "which live in one and the same code base",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.50999999999999,
          "end": 101.12299999999999,
          "en": "and still can adapt to different environments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.45,
          "end": 104.53,
          "en": "Now, for this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.53,
          "end": 106.55,
          "en": "I wanna build up on the app we built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.55,
          "end": 108.4,
          "en": "in the previous course section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.4,
          "end": 111.94,
          "en": "and therefore you find the code of that finished app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.94,
          "end": 114.8,
          "en": "which we built in the previous section attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.8,
          "end": 117.65,
          "en": "to this lecture so that we can all start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.65,
          "end": 119.363,
          "en": "with the same code base.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.27,
          "end": 123.2,
          "en": "Now, here is the app running on iOS and Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.2,
          "end": 127.39,
          "en": "And I would say the look and the layout is quite good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.39,
          "end": 131.053,
          "en": "There isn't anything obvious that I would want to change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.97,
          "end": 136.92000000000002,
          "en": "But, of course, not all our users are going to use one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.92000000000002,
          "end": 139.91,
          "en": "of the latest iPhones or Android devices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.91,
          "end": 144.47,
          "en": "instead they might be using older or smaller devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.47,
          "end": 148.487,
          "en": "And our app typically should be able to adjust to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.487,
          "end": 151.78,
          "en": "And we wanna adjust our look and feel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.78,
          "end": 155.66,
          "en": "For example, here I also started an Android emulator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.66,
          "end": 158.86,
          "en": "based on the Nexus 5 image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.86,
          "end": 163.61,
          "en": "And I'll close the more recent pixel three device emulator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.61,
          "end": 166.12,
          "en": "Now this is a fine Android device",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.12,
          "end": 169.63,
          "en": "but as you can clearly tell, it is a bit smaller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.63,
          "end": 172.7,
          "en": "If I resize this, it just gets bigger here on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.7,
          "end": 177.13,
          "en": "but if we talk about available pixels, it is smaller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 177.13,
          "end": 179.53,
          "en": "It has less space available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 179.53,
          "end": 181.47,
          "en": "And if that would be a real device,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.47,
          "end": 183.28,
          "en": "the screen would be smaller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.28,
          "end": 185.6,
          "en": "We can tell that everything is smaller",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.6,
          "end": 188.363,
          "en": "because everything is bigger here on the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.3,
          "end": 192.27,
          "en": "And the starting screen still looks all right,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.27,
          "end": 196.9,
          "en": "but if we dive into the game, we notice some differences.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.9,
          "end": 200.01,
          "en": "For example, the title is right at the top here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.01,
          "end": 203.23,
          "en": "It's really at the edge of this screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.23,
          "end": 206.75,
          "en": "because this device is smaller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.75,
          "end": 211.29,
          "en": "Now, if we play this game here until it's over,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.29,
          "end": 214.41,
          "en": "then we see that also on this game over screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.41,
          "end": 216.84,
          "en": "Yeah, it fits on one screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.84,
          "end": 220.26,
          "en": "but the title is really already a little bit below",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.26,
          "end": 223.45,
          "en": "the status bar and everything probably",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.45,
          "end": 227.673,
          "en": "is a little bit too big for this small of a device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.71,
          "end": 231.26,
          "en": "So therefore we might wanna adjust some",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.26,
          "end": 235.16,
          "en": "of our style settings, some of our layout styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 235.16,
          "end": 240.16,
          "en": "such that the app looks a bit better on smaller devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.2,
          "end": 243.1,
          "en": "And that's what we're going to start with in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
